  "final_output": "## Root cause\nThe 10:34 UTC Auth canary config cut the local Users Postgres connection pool from 12 to 2. Two session listeners held both connections. Interactive requests on that replica waited 250 ms for a connection and returned 503 before issuing SQL.\n\n## Evidence\nGateway route samples show 503s on login, refresh, and signup. Trace 8bd0e59997bc08dcff6ae97ad5ea01ee ends at pool acquisition. The settings log records the reduced pool and both listeners. Users Postgres stayed up and its query latency and connection usage stayed low.\n\n## Customer impact\nSome customers could not log in, refresh a session, or sign up from 10:34 to 10:56 UTC. Login success fell to roughly half per minute. Successful Auth requests continued on the other replica and checkout processing stayed healthy.\n\n## Next steps\nThe 10:56 UTC rollback restored 12 pool connections and the gateway and Auth alerts cleared. No immediate action is needed. Verify login and refresh stay healthy and reserve capacity for request traffic before rolling out these settings again."
